From: Brad Barnett <127794626+bdbarnett@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 01:23:40 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] esp32/machine_i2s: Clock I2S from the APLL on the ESP32-S31.

The S31's default I2S clock source is its 40 MHz crystal, which no audio
rate divides. The fractional divider then moves each bit clock edge by up
to a crystal cycle, and a codec that clocks itself from BCLK (the ES8389
on the Waveshare S31-Touch-LCD-4.3C) plays hiss over everything on about
two opens in three.
---
 ports/esp32/machine_i2s.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ports/esp32/machine_i2s.c b/ports/esp32/machine_i2s.c
index 2c02c0b..d3e0a57 100644
--- a/ports/esp32/machine_i2s.c
+++ b/ports/esp32/machine_i2s.c
@@ -481,6 +481,11 @@ static void mp_machine_i2s_init_helper(machine_i2s_obj_t *self, mp_arg_val_t *ar
             },
         },
     };
+    #if CONFIG_IDF_TARGET_ESP32S31
+    // The default I2S clock here is the 40 MHz crystal, which no audio rate
+    // divides; the APLL gives an even bit clock.
+    std_cfg.clk_cfg.clk_src = I2S_CLK_SRC_APLL;
+    #endif
 
     if (mode == MICROPY_PY_MACHINE_I2S_CONSTANT_TX) {
         std_cfg.gpio_cfg.dout = self->sd;
-- 
